An operator who exposes Skeid as the public model API (api.<domain>) wants machine-readable documentation from day one, generated from what the proxy actually serves instead of written by hand.

What exists: the routes are listed in the POD of Langertha::Skeid::Proxy (GET /v1/models, /v1/chat/completions, /v1/embeddings, /v1/audio/*, /v1/rerank, the Anthropic and Ollama faces, /skeid admin). There is no OpenAPI document and no UI.

Wanted:
- GET /openapi.json: OpenAPI 3.1 for the client-facing routes that are enabled in this configuration (a face that is switched off does not appear). Admin routes under /skeid stay out, or go into a separate document behind the admin key.
- A Swagger UI (or equivalent) under one path, switchable off, served without pulling assets from a CDN.
- The security scheme documents client_auth (bearer key).
- Model names in the examples come from the same source as GET /v1/models.

Done when: the document validates against OpenAPI 3.1, a test fails when a client-facing route is added without an entry, and the UI can list models and send one chat request with a key.

